From: khristophe972-glitch <khristophe972@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: compat: define cfg80211 NAN sched constants for 6.18

mt76 be5ce7910521 (2026-09-01) embeds NAN peer-schedule state in
mt792x_sta_nan_sched / mt792x_nan, sizing arrays with
CFG80211_NAN_SCHED_NUM_TIME_SLOTS (32) and CFG80211_NAN_MAX_PEER_MAPS (2).
Those constants were added to include/net/cfg80211.h by the post-6.18 NAN
schedule API and do not exist on kernel 6.18, breaking mt7921 compilation:

  mt7921/../mt792x.h:136: error: 'CFG80211_NAN_SCHED_NUM_TIME_SLOTS'
  undeclared here (not in a function)

The NAN schedule feature itself lives in mt7925 (not built on this target),
so defining the two constants here is sufficient; values match mainline.
Local kernel-compat patch: drop once the tree kernel exposes the cfg80211
NAN peer-schedule API.
--- a/mt792x.h	2026-09-04 14:16:56.263514707 +0200
+++ b/mt792x.h	2026-09-04 14:21:29.998144504 +0200
@@ -11,6 +11,16 @@
 #include "mt792x_regs.h"
 #include "mt792x_acpi_sar.h"
 
+/* cfg80211 NAN peer-schedule API is post-6.18: provide the constants that
+ * size the NAN structs mt7921 embeds (the feature itself lives in mt7925,
+ * which is not built on 6.18). */
+#ifndef CFG80211_NAN_SCHED_NUM_TIME_SLOTS
+#define CFG80211_NAN_SCHED_NUM_TIME_SLOTS 32
+#endif
+#ifndef CFG80211_NAN_MAX_PEER_MAPS
+#define CFG80211_NAN_MAX_PEER_MAPS 2
+#endif
+
 #define MT792x_PM_TIMEOUT	(HZ / 12)
 #define MT792x_HW_SCAN_TIMEOUT	(HZ / 10)
 
